/*--------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  FIXED-PRESSURE BINARY BUBBLE-POINT EVIDENCE, extracted from a ThermoML
  file by bin/choupo-thermoml extract-vle.

  system       ethanol + water   (x1 is ethanol)
  pressure     101.3 kPa   (CONSTANT across the series)
  points       21

  The identity below is DECLARED AS FIELDS, not only described here:
  a header is a comment the parser discards, and the dossier must be
  able to say which archive file, which publication and which system
  a verdict rests on.

  The role this evidence plays -- fit or held-out validation -- is NOT
  set here.  It is declared in the operation that consumes it, before
  any fitting runs (src/propertyOps/EvidencePartition.H).

  CHECKED AGAINST THE ARTICLE, 2026-08-25.  Every value below was read
  back against Table 3 of the cited paper (Kamihama, Matsuda, Kurihara,
  Tochigi & Oba, J. Chem. Eng. Data 57 (2012) 339-344) -- the DOI in the
  article's own running footer confirming the one declared here.  All 21
  rows agree digit for digit AND in order: Table 3 carries 23 rows, of
  which 21 lie strictly inside 0 < x1 < 1.

  THE ENDPOINTS ARE DELIBERATELY ABSENT, for the reason given in the
  companion fit set: a bubble point on a pure component measures the
  Antoine fit, not the pair being scored.
\*--------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

property     binaryVLE.T_bubble;
system       ( ethanol water );
pressure     101.3 kPa;

provenance
{
    source       measured;
    reviewStatus checked;
    archiveFile  "je2008704.xml";
    doi          "10.1021/je2008704";
    sha256       "f24eca1286fb3d1fc4611eaf05bc771813d0dc41e81cf37c0c49b3ea9b871758";
}

columns
(
    { name x1;  unit -;  }
    { name T;   unit K;  }
);

data
(
      0.0180  368.18
      0.0790  360.5
      0.0900  359.7
      0.1470  357.27
      0.2440  355.38
      0.3110  354.55
